Growing up, I was taught to check my weather before going out. *Who knows?* Maybe rain is coming in a few hours time. I have always been very reliant on weather forecast to plan my activities; and to use forecast to drop out of things I don't actually want to do early.

About 9 years ago I moved to Singapore. It's a place where rainfall is proper unpredictable. Unless it is monsoon seasons (when it just rain for a few days straight), the rain can come in quite suddenly. You only get to find out on the day.

To be fair, the Singapore government maintains an excellent site to provide a variety of forecasts. Real time rainfall radar map, 2-hour forecast, 4-day outlook, and more. They have maintained even better open data source of the same in the event you require the data for research or development purposes.

My only complain was with the user experience of their website...

